  "adjudication_note": "A uniform draw from the occurrences the risk queue had dismissed found four errors and all four were the same shape: the Portuguese material quotes English terms verbatim, and a bare English label matches a fragment of one. `Hedge Funds` is not a hedge; `Money Weighted Rate of Return` is not money; `Dow Jones Industrial Average` is not an average. scripts/find_compound_fragments.py then mapped the whole cluster — 31 forms, 155 events — by measuring what surrounds each match instead of what context it sits in, which is why the centroid ranking was blind to it. The repair is not to forbid the fragments. Every one of these compounds is CGA exam content that the dictionary should contain, and once the compound is registered the longest-match rule consumes it and the fragment stops appearing. Suppression would have shrunk the registry to fix a problem whose correct answer was to grow it. `hedge funds` is not in this batch: the concept already exists and only lacked its plural, so it is an amendment rather than a new concept — adding one would have split a sense in two.",
